// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - Dialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - DialogStartPage 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SaysList :
"P1521345202" "<t=4 caption x= 0.6 y=0.5 d=4><scale 1.75><color deepskyblue><bgcolor white> {HeroName}, this is Parson. Can you hear me? <t=8 caption x= 0.6 y=0.5 d=8><scale 1.75><color deepskyblue><bgcolor white>Great. Alright, the Clockwork haven't reacted to you yet. I'll make sure the doors to the signal carrier are unlocked for you. <t=6 caption x= 0.6 y=0.5 d=6><scale 1.75><color deepskyblue><bgcolor white>I also designated the signal carrier's location. You shouldn't have any trouble finding him."
// SaysList :
"P3919597921" "<t=5 caption x= 0.6 y=0.5 d=5><scale 1.75><color deepskyblue><bgcolor white> {HeroName}, I'm picking up some strange energy signatures in the lab.<t=5 caption x= 0.6 y=0.5  d=5><scale 1.75><color deepskyblue><bgcolor white>The Clockwork are reacting to your arrival, {HeroName}. Be careful."
// SaysList :
"P1146235128" "<t=5 caption x= 0.6 y=0.5 d=5><scale 1.75><color deepskyblue><bgcolor white> {HeroName}, the Clockwork are accessing the MICIR mainframe!<t=5 caption x= 0.6 y=0.5  d=5><scale 1.75><color deepskyblue><bgcolor white>This isn't a random malfunction, they're trying to steal classified information!<t=5 caption x= 0.6 y=0.5  d=5><scale 1.75><color deepskyblue><bgcolor white>Shut down the signal carrier! It's the fastest way to stop them! "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4274256517" "Alec Parson tells you something important."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1997753402" "You've disabled the signal carrier and returned the malfunctioning Clockwork back to normal operating parameters."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1265653687" "Great job, {HeroName}, it looks like you managed to deactivate the signal carrier before it could transmit any data. I just hope you left enough of it intact for me to sift through the memory banks and see what it was after."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3986203640" "{HeroName}. We lucked out. Despite trying to self destruct it looks like you managed to keep the Clockwork from completely destroying its memory chips. I sifted around through its memory and compared what pieces I could find with its path through our databases.<br><br>It looks like it was doing some shopping. Turns out it was very interested in <color yellow>Imperial Storage</color>, a storage depot for Clockwork parts. <color orange>I think it would be a good idea to get down there and see if whoever was behind that strange signal shows up.</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P2663402780" "Check out Imperial Storage"
// SendOffString :
"P1080841122" "Oh, before I forget. I analyzed the files in the memory chips of all the Clockwork that were subjected to that carrier signal. You know, searching for any sort of hacking or file rewrites. Amazingly there were none, with one notable exception.<br><br>I found an entirely new data file in the memory of the signal carrier. It was a <color yellow>schematic for a Clockwork design</color>, one I've never seen before.<br><br>Maybe I'm not giving this the gravity it deserves. You see, this schematic is far more advanced than anything I have ever seen! It makes amazing use of simple modifications to commonly existing parts. The design achieves staggering results. Frankly, I feel kinda inept that I didn't see it before, it's all so obvious seeing it all laid out like that.<br><br>{HeroName}, I'm very interested in testing these schematics out, but I have a feeling whoever embedded that file is going to make a grab for the parts first. <color orange>I want you to stop them and bring the parts to me.</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3546440258" "Retrieve components from Imperial Storage"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P683281527" "You need to get over to Imperial Storage and grab those Clockwork parts for me before whoever is behind this gets them."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P4078136732" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: Pieces Parts</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P4109204161" "From the sound of it, you aren't the first one here."

